# Russian: the rules the formant voice speaks it by (docs/tts.md,
# "Other languages"). Written from Russian spelling, read as it is spelled: the iotated vowels, -ого, -ться, final devoicing, but no vowel reduction, because stress is not written -- it is guessed (the last syllable after a consonant, else the second-last), and ё always takes it.
name Russian
stress penult
last-if-ends бвгджзйклмнпрстфхцчшщь
unstressed 2
vowels аеёиоуыэюя
weak и в во с со к ко на о об у а но не же бы ли из за по до от

